      {
        "id": 89483,
        "name": "PlatinumWarlock",
        "username": "PlatinumWarlock",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/platinumwarlock/{size}/1869_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-02-06T06:03:51.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I'd liken it more to Marvel's \"<a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Acts_of_vengeance\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">Acts of Vengeance</a>\" storyline, which was specifically about various villains teaming up and trading off to taken down the Avengers one-by-one. &nbsp;</p><p>A similar storyline took place in the recent animated film&nbsp;<a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justice_League_Doom\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"><em>Justice League: Doom</em></a>, which dealt with very similar themes. &nbsp;It was based loosely on the \"<a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/JLA:_Tower_of_Babel\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">Tower of Babel</a>\" storyline, replacing Ra's al-Ghul with Vandal Savage.</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
